title: config-service zone loss, no failover
description: Disaster recovery test of the config store of the docs pictures that does not recover. The store is lost and nothing brings it back while the run watches, so the run breaches its RTO with the time it watched as a lower bound. The rollback restores the backup. The lab is a folder of files that data.py makes.

tags[2]: dr, zone-loss
kind: dr
target:
  system: config-service
  technology: configuration
  environment: demo
rto_target_s: 10
recovery:
  window_s: 12
  interval_s: 1

steady_state_hypothesis:
  title: The config store answers
  probes[1]:
    - name: store-answers
      activity_type: probe
      provider:
        type: process
        path: sh
        arguments[3]: "${lab}/lab.sh", "${lab}", up
        timeout_s: 5.0
      tolerance:
        type: regex
        pattern: "^up$"

method[1]:
  - name: lose-the-zone
    activity_type: action
    provider:
      type: process
      path: sh
      arguments[2]: "-c", "rm -f '${lab}/up' '${lab}/store' && echo the store is gone"
      timeout_s: 5.0

rollbacks[1]:
  - name: restore-the-backup
    activity_type: action
    provider:
      type: process
      path: sh
      arguments[3]: "${lab}/lab.sh", "${lab}", restore
      timeout_s: 5.0
